# A terrain proof: an open hilltop clearing on a surface map, its ground given
# relief by a baked heightmap. The HM_HILL lump is a radial gradient, so the
# centre rises into a rounded hill and the edges fall away. The logical grid is
# flat and open, so movement and collision are unchanged; only the rendered
# ground has height. 1=wall (a ring of cliff), 0=open ground.
map OVERLOOK
size 20 20
tileset 2
surface
area forest
# the clearing's ground rises toward the centre: sample 0 sits at world height 0,
# sample 255 at 48/16 = 3 world units
heightmap HM_HILL 0 48
walls
11111111111111111111
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
10000000000000000001
11111111111111111111
end
marker start 3 16 N
marker back 3 16 N
portal 1 16 DUNGEON back
